  "notes": "{雑然|ざつぜん} is a taru-adjective describing a state of disorder or clutter.\n\nCOMMON PATTERNS:\n- {雑然|ざつぜん}とした + noun: cluttered ~\n- {雑然|ざつぜん}としている: to be in a cluttered state\n- {雑然|ざつぜん}と + verb: in a disorderly manner\n\nSIMILAR WORDS:\n- {整然|せいぜん}: orderly, neat\n\nRELATED WORDS:\n- {雑多|ざった}: miscellaneous (emphasis on variety rather than disorder)\n- {散|ち}らかる: to be scattered, messy\n\nCOMMON COLLOCATIONS:\n- {雑然|ざつぜん}とした{部屋|へや}: a cluttered room\n- {雑然|ざつぜん}とした{状態|じょうたい}: a state of disorder",
